from pathlib import Path
import html,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;d=json.loads((R/'RESULTS.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
e=lambda x:html.escape(str(x))
def table(head,rows):return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(h)+'</th>' for h in head)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(v)+'</td>' for v in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
def line(ev):return '<article><p><strong>'+e(ev['locator'])+'</strong> · middle ordinal '+str(ev['ordinal'])+'</p><p class="raw">'+' '.join('□' if w is None else '<mark>'+e(w)+'</mark>' if w=='shedy' else e(w) for w in ev['tokens'])+'</p></article>'
body='<p class="muted">VOYNICH · SHARED-FRAME TEST · v69</p><h1>Is shedy ___ shedy unusually recurrent?</h1><p class="notice">Total frame frequency and recurrence of distinct middle words are tested separately. Results are conditional on the chosen null. No middle word is assigned an operation, attribute, timing or medicinal meaning.</p>'
body+='<p>Bath section · hand 2 · Currier B · raw P. Original numbered folio f75 excluded, as in v61/v66. Same eligible H/F source loci, with readings counted separately. Exposed corpus; retrospective evidence.</p>'
rows=[]
for p in d['panels']:
 for x in p['results']:
  rows.append([p['reading'],e(p['mode']),'Occurrences T' if x['statistic']=='total_frame_occurrences' else 'Recurring middle types R',x['observed'],f'{x["null_mean"]:.3f}',e([round(n,2) for n in x['null_95']]),f'{x["p_raw"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_all_frames_max"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_eight_panels"]:.4f}','Pass' if x['observed']>x['null_mean'] and x['p_eight_panels']<=.05 else 'Does not pass'])
body+='<h2>Frequency and shared-middle recurrence</h2>'+table(['Reading','Control','Statistic','Observed','Null mean','Central 95% null range','Raw p','All-frame max p','Eight-panel p','Frozen screen'],rows)
body+='<p>T counts complete readable <code>shedy X shedy</code> triples. R counts distinct middle words each appearing in that frame on at least two numbered folios. The null range describes shuffled scores, not an effect-size confidence interval. P-values are plus-one Monte Carlo estimates from 1,999 shuffles.</p>'
passing=[p['reading']+' '+p['mode']+' '+x['statistic'] for p in d['panels'] for x in p['results'] if x['observed']>x['null_mean'] and x['p_eight_panels']<=.05]
body+='<p class="notice"><strong>Results passing the frozen full screen:</strong> '+e('; '.join(passing) or 'none')+'. Preserve differences between controls; a sensitivity result does not replace the primary exact-position result.</p>'
if (R/'MC-UNCERTAINTY.json').exists():
 mc=json.loads((R/'MC-UNCERTAINTY.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
 body+='<p><strong>Finite-shuffle uncertainty:</strong> the H within-line R result has only 8 all-frame-max exceedances among 1,999 shuffles. Its eight-panel adjusted point estimate is .036, but a post-run exact-binomial Monte Carlo interval for the adjusted tail probability is approximately .014–.063. This crosses .05. It is a narrow numerical screen pass, not a stable shared-reading conclusion. No extra shuffles were added or tests changed. <a href="MC-UNCERTAINTY.json">All Monte Carlo uncertainty intervals</a>.</p>'
body+='<h2>What is held constant?</h2><p><strong>Exact position, primary:</strong> exchange all readable words between slots on the same page with identical line length, exact ordinal and unknown-slot mask. Page/position-conditioned word counts remain fixed. Source-line word multisets need not remain fixed.</p><p><strong>Within line, sensitivity:</strong> shuffle readable interior spans within each line; endpoints and unknown barriers stay fixed. Every line retains its words, but non-endpoint exact ordinals may change.</p><p>No shedy positions are specially locked. Locking both flanks would preserve the number of open frames by construction and could not test their recurrence.</p>'
body+='<h2>Search correction and mobility</h2><p>Every shuffle searches <strong>all ordered left/right flank-word pairs</strong>, including unequal flanks and every middle word. Its highest T and R set the corresponding selection-adjusted thresholds. These raw maxima can be driven by common frames, making this correction conservative. A further factor of eight covers two readings × two controls × two statistics. This does not correct every earlier research decision or establish untouched confirmation.</p>'
body+=table(['Reading/control','Movable word slots','Observed target-frame unique slots','Movable target-frame slots'],[[e(p['reading']+' / '+p['mode']),p['mobility']['movable_word_slots'],p['mobility']['observed_frame_unique_slots'],p['mobility']['movable_observed_frame_slots']] for p in d['panels']])
body+='<h2>Every observed middle word · exceptions included</h2><p>The earlier v66 frame table considered only words already in qol’s neighbour inventory. This test admits <em>every</em> readable middle word. That expands the totals from 8/8 to 10 H / 11 F without changing the three cross-folio recurring middle types. Extra one-folio words are preserved.</p>'
words=sorted(set(d['observed']['H']['members'])|set(d['observed']['F']['members']))
body+=table(['Middle word','H count / folios','F count / folios'],[[e(w)]+[str(d['observed'][tr]['members'][w]['count'])+' / '+str(d['observed'][tr]['members'][w]['folios']) if w in d['observed'][tr]['members'] else '0 / 0' for tr in ['H','F']] for w in words])
for tr in ['H','F']:
 o=d['observed'][tr];body+='<h2>'+tr+' · full source passages</h2>'
 for w,v in o['members'].items():body+='<details open><summary>'+e(w)+' · '+str(v['count'])+' occurrences / '+str(v['folios'])+' folios'+(' · cross-folio recurring' if v['folios']>=2 else ' · one-folio exception')+'</summary>'+''.join(line(ev) for ev in v['events'])+'</details>'
 body+='<details><summary>Unknown middle slots · '+str(len(o['unknown_middle']))+'</summary>'+''.join(line(ev) for ev in o['unknown_middle'])+'</details>'
 body+='<details><summary>Background opportunities with only one shedy flank · '+str(len(o['one_flank_background']))+' token windows</summary><p>These are background contexts, not violations of an established grammatical rule. Unknown slots remain unknown; source lines are not joined.</p>'+''.join(line(ev) for ev in o['one_flank_background'])+'</details>'
 body+='<details><summary>All observed flank frames · '+str(len(o['all_frames']))+'</summary>'+table(['Left','Right','T','R'],[[e(x['left']),e(x['right']),x['T'],x['R']] for x in o['all_frames']])+'</details>'
body+='<h2>Engineering checks and interpretation</h2><p>Both shuffle schemes preserve their declared bucket multisets, unknown-slot positions and frequency/position controls. A hand-worked example checks frame and recurring-middle counting. The pre-run synthetic T diagnostics are shown below; they do not qualify R sensitivity, historical text or semantics.</p>'+table(['Control','Exchangeable flags / 20','Planted T detections / 20'],[[e(q['mode']),q['null_flags'],q['planted_T_detections']] for q in d['qualification']])
body+='<p>A supported frame arrangement would constrain later hypotheses about use. It would not identify the middle words as operations, attributes or time expressions. Disagreement between nulls is part of the result. A failed conservative screen does not establish that the manuscript lacks reusable slots.</p><p><a href="RESULTS.json">All results and background contexts</a> · <a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen protocol</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Method/input hashes</a> · <a href="QUALIFICATION.json">Engineering diagnostics</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Numerical verification</a> · <a href="../neighbor-patterns-v66/report.html">Original frame discovery</a></p><p>Source fidelity and numerical replay are checked separately from browser appearance. Browser visual review was not performed.</p>'
css='''<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:light-dark(#f5f2e9,#18251f);--fg:light-dark(#203f35,#e2e9df);--sub:light-dark(#54695b,#b4c7b7);--rule:light-dark(#c0ccbd,#48604d);--fill:light-dark(#e5ebda,#2a3e2d);--mark:light-dark(#e6edb7,#526330)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1450px;padding:30px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:30px}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:inherit}.muted{color:var(--sub)}.notice{padding:16px;background:var(--fill)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.raw{font:15px/1.8 ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}mark{background:var(--mark);color:inherit}article{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:16px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}}</style>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Shared shedy frame versus frequency and position · v69</title>'+css+'</head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8')
print('Shared-frame report written.')
